  [already_present] context-blocks-have-no-requirement-id-or-disposition/deeper-mandate-heading-swallowed-into-context
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 112 skipped once the defect was covered
    Lines 96-97 skip every heading deeper than the Context heading without resetting `section` or `context_level`. So a later `### Task` or `### Constraints` stays in context, and its blocks go to `result.context` with no requirement id. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair stops skipping a deeper heading when it names a mandate section, so `section` is reset by the normal path. I could not see `_TASK` or `_list_target`, so I assumed `_TASK` holds the task-section names and `_list_target` returns None for sections that are not mandate. The repair depends on those assumptions.

