  [already_present] context-does-not-move-coverage-counts/context-text-drives-obligations
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 112 skipped once the defect was covered
    Line 555 in `_user_prompt` splices `_context_block(context or [])` into every per-requirement prompt. `decompose` passes `parsed.context` into every `_ask_about` call (lines 1159 and 1218). The Context text therefore reaches the decomposer as prompt content, and the only guard is a sentence in the prompt saying it is not a requirement. So the decomposer can derive obligations or change dispositions from it, and the counts can differ with and without Context. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The smallest repair is to drop the context block from the prompt, so the outcome no longer depends on whether Context is present.

